It's very dark, and you can't see further than at arm's length. You can hear some animals moving up and down the adjacent trees; you are becoming a bit nervous. No one can guarantee that all predators of the island are unable to climb trees. Still, the decision is made, and there is no way to change it.

Suddenly, a loud roaring, snapping of twigs, and a heartrending screech are heard from below. Soon the screech stops, replaced by blood-chilling silence, and you hear horrible sounds of flesh being torn apart. It looks like some large predator caught its prey. You press yourself to the trunk of the tree, trying not to make any noise. Horrible sounds subside soon. After some time, the night is full of sounds again, made by forest inhabitants. Your eyes are becoming heavy, your mind is getting clouded... You fall asleep.